{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) is requesting implementation of Task #5475: `[stitch] cmd/od: srd072 R1.1-R1.4`. This is a code generation task to create the `od` (octal dump) utility for the go-unix-utils project. The scope is limited to requirements R1.1 through R1.4 from the SRD, covering default behavior and type specifiers. Two files must be created: `cmd/od/main.go` and `cmd/od/od_test.go`. The implementation must pass differential tests against the GNU `god` reference binary.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing**: Compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`god`) using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **od utility**: Dumps file contents in octal, hex, decimal, or character formats\n   - **Type specifiers (-t TYPE)**: Format letters a/c/d/f/o/u/x with optional byte size\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - **Default format**: Octal 2-byte words (`-t o2`) with octal address offset column\n   - **Multiple type specifiers**: Each `-t` option adds an additional output line per input block\n   - **File/stdin input**: Read from FILE args in order, or stdin when no file or \"-\" given\n   - **Function size limit**: 40 lines max (E8), file size limit 500 lines (E9)\n   - **Copyright header**: Required on every Go file\n   - **pkg/sizeparse**: Listed in package_contract for parsing byte count suffixes\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd072-od.yaml** (READ)\n     - Full SRD for the od utility with 4 requirement groups (R1-R4)\n     - Task only covers R1.1-R1.4 (default behavior and type specifiers)\n     - R1.1: Default format is octal 2-byte words with octal addresses\n     - R1.2: `-t TYPE` / `--format=TYPE` for format letters (a,c,d,f,o,u,x) + optional size\n     - R1.3: Multiple `-t` options produce additional lines per block\n     - R1.4: Read from FILE args or stdin when no file/\"-\" given\n     - Non-goals: no `--strings`/`-S`, no `--endian`\n     - Package contract imports: `pkg/sizeparse` and `pkg/sys`\n   \n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (PROVIDED in project_context)\n     - Full differential testing framework source code\n     - Key exports: `DiffTest` struct, `RunDiffTests()`, `BuildBinary()`, `ComposeNormalizers()`, `TimestampNormalizer`\n     - `DiffTest` fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` runs each test as subtest\n     - `buildEnv()` merges test env with LC_ALL=C default\n\n   - **cmd/od/main.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - od utility implementation covering R1.1-R1.4\n   \n   - **cmd/od/od_test.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests using `god` reference binary\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full specification before implementing\n   - Identified that the task scope is R1.1-R1.4 only, but a functional od needs some address output (R2.4) and basic infrastructure to produce meaningful test output\n   - The design decisions specify using `god` as reference binary via `exec.LookPath`\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed task description including role, repository files listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts. The core request is to implement `cmd/od` for srd072 R1.1-R1.4.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do