{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EvbyBN5pojWwdf88xtaVcD","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information needed. Let me create a comprehensive summary report.\n\n## Summary Report: Go Unix Utils Code Patterns and Style Guide\n\n### 1. COPYRIGHT HEADER FORMAT\n\nAll Go files start with a two-line SPDX copyright header, followed by a blank line, then the package declaration:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n```\n\nThis applies to all Go files: cmd/, pkg/, and internal/. The header is mandatory.\n\n### 2. FLAG PARSING APPROACH\n\n**Two patterns are used depending on complexity:**\n\n**Simple utilities (cat, echo):** Manual flag parsing with custom parseFlags/applyFlag functions\n- Direct iteration through args\n- Custom loop-based parsing for short flags (-abc combines multiple single flags)\n- Simple switch statements for flag recognition\n- Used in: cmd/cat/main.go, cmd/echo/main.go\n\n**Complex utilities (numfmt, head, wc):** stdlib `flag` package for some, manual parsing for others\n- cmd/numfmt/main.go uses `flag.String`, `flag.Int`, etc. from stdlib\n- cmd/head/main.go uses custom parseLongFlag/parseShortFlags with dedicated arg handling\n- cmd/wc/main.go also uses custom parsing but with long-flag support (--lines=, --bytes=)\n- No pflag dependency; standard library only\n\nExample from cmd/cat (simple pattern):\n```go\nfunc parseFlags(args []string) []string {\n    var files []string\n    endOfFlags := false\n    for _, arg := range args {\n        if endOfFlags || arg == \"\" || arg == \"-\" || arg[0] != '-' {\n            files = append(files, arg)\n            continue\n        }\n        if arg == \"--\" {\n            endOfFlags = true\n            continue\n        }\n        for _, c := range arg[1:] {\n            applyFlag(c)\n        }\n    }\n    return files\n}\n```\n\nExample from cmd/head (more complex pattern):\n```go\nfunc parseLongFlag(flag string, remaining []string, opts *options) (int, error) {\n    switch {\n    case flag == \"--help\":\n        fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n        os.Exit(0)\n        return 0, nil\n    case strings.HasPrefix(flag, \"--lines=\"):\n        count, err := parseLineCount(flag[len(\"--lines=\"):])\n        // ... handle\n        return 1, nil\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3. MAIN.GO STRUCTURE\n\nAll cmd/ utilities follow a consistent pattern:\n\n1. **Copyright header** (lines 1-3)\n2. **Package declaration with comment** (lines 4-6) - often includes SRD reference\n3. **Imports** (lines 8-17) - organized in groups: stdlib, then github.com packages\n4. **Global variables** (if needed) - flags and constants\n5. **func main()** - entry point:\n   - **First line**: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - critical for piping behavior\n   - Parse arguments\n   - Set defaults\n   - Call helper functions to execute work\n   - Handle errors and set exit code\n6. **Helper functions** - named, focused functions for each responsibility\n\nExample structure from cmd/cat/main.go:\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"bufio\"\n    \"errors\"\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"syscall\"\n    \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\nvar (\n    flagN bool\n    flagB bool\n    // ... other flags\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n    sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n    args := parseFlags(os.Args[1:])\n    // ... parse, execute, handle errors\n}\n\n// Helper functions follow...\n```\n\n### 4. KEY OBSERVATIONS ABOUT sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5475/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\n**Signature:**\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n    c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n    signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n    go func() {\n        <-c\n        os.Exit(0)\n    }()\n}\n```\n\n- Must be called at the start of main()\n- Matches GNU coreutils behavior when piped to consumers that close early\n- Safe to call multiple times (each invocation starts one goroutine)\n- Uses signal.Notify with buffered channel (not signal.Ignore)\n\n### 5. pkg/sizeparse EXPORTS\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5475/pkg/sizeparse/parse.go`\n\n**Key functions:**\n```go\n// ParseOptions configures size string parsing\ntype ParseOptions struct {\n    AllowSign   bool  // permits +/- prefix\n    DefaultUnit int64 // multiplier when no suffix\n}\n\n// Parse parses human-readable size (delegates to ParseWithOptions with defaults)\nfunc Parse(s string) (int64, error)\n\n// ParseWithOptions parses with configurable options\nfunc ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error)\n```\n\n**Supported suffixes:** b (512), K/KiB (1024), KB (1000), M/MiB (1<<20), MB (1M), G/GiB (1<<30), GB (1B), T/TiB (1<<40), TB, P/PiB (1<<50), PB, E/EiB (1<<60), EB\n\n**Usage example from cmd/head:**\n```go\nimport \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\"\n\nfunc parseByteCount(s string) (int64, error) {\n    n, err := sizeparse.ParseWithOptions(s, sizeparse.ParseOptions{AllowSign: true})\n    if err != nil {\n        return 0, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid number of bytes: '%s'\", s)\n    }\n    return n, nil\n}\n```\n\n### 6. TEST FILE STRUCTURE\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5475/cmd/cat/cat_test.go`\n\n**Pattern: Differential Testing**\n\n```go\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"bytes\"\n    \"context\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"os/exec\"\n    \"path/filepath\"\n    \"testing\"\n    \"time\"\n    \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n    goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n    refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gcat\")  // GNU reference with g-prefix\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Skip(\"reference binary gcat not found\")\n    }\n    tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n        {Name: \"test_name\", Stdin: []byte(\"data\")},\n        {Name: \"another_test\", Args: []string{\"-flag\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"data\")},\n        // ...\n    }\n    testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n\n// Additional non-differential tests can follow\nfunc TestSIGPIPE(t *testing.T) {\n    goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n    // ... test SIGPIPE handling\n}\n```\n\n**Key DiffTest struct fields:**\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n    Name          string        // subtest name for t.Run\n    Args          []string      // command-line args\n    Stdin         []byte        // nil = EOF immediately, []byte{} = open then close\n    Env           []string      // merged into inherited env; LC_ALL=C is default\n    WorkDir       string        // working directory (temp dir if empty)\n    ExitCode      int           // expected exit code (default 0)\n    Normalize     []NormalizeFunc // transformation funcs before comparison\n    ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte // check created files\n}\n```\n\n### 7. PACKAGE STRUCTURE (pkg/sys and pkg/testutils)\n\n**pkg/sys exports:**\n- `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - signal handling\n- `OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))` - SIGWINCH handler\n- `TerminalWidth() (int, error)` - get terminal width\n- File info helpers (fileinfo.go)\n- Platform-specific stat functions (stat_darwin.go, etc.)\n\n**pkg/testutils exports:**\n- `BuildBinary(t *testing.T, path string) string` - compile cmd package, return binary path\n- `RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)` - run differential tests\n- `DiffTest` struct - test case definition\n- `NormalizeFunc` - func([]byte) []byte for output normalization\n- `TimestampNormalizer` - built-in normalizer for timestamp tests\n- `ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc` - combine normalizers\n\n### 8. CODE STYLE CONSTRAINTS (from docs/constitutions)\n\n**From go-style.yaml:**\n\n1. **Copyright header** - mandatory on lines 1-2 before package\n2. **Duplication threshold is 2** - if code appears twice, extract to shared function\n3. **Implementation strategy** - write all files before building, plan fully, minimize turns\n4. **Function size limit (E8)** - no function may exceed 40 lines of code\n5. **File size limit (E9)** - files should stay under 500 lines; split by responsibility when exceeded\n6. **No interface{}/any** - every value must have concrete type or named interface\n7. **Small interfaces** - 1-3 methods per interface\n8. **Accept interfaces as parameters, return concrete structs**\n9. **Struct embedding for field sharing**\n10. **DRY enforcement (E10)** - extract if code repeats\n\n**From execution.yaml (critical constraints):**\n\n1. **E1 - Specification-first** - code must match SRDs and ARCHITECTURE, don't invent patterns\n2. **E2 - Traceability** - commit messages reference SRD implementations\n3. **E3 - No scope creep** - only modify listed files, no extra features\n4. **E4 - Session completion** - work complete when files written and tests pass, NO git commands\n5. **E6 - Non-goals enforcement** - don't implement features in SRD non_goals\n6. **E8 - Function size hard limit** - 40 lines max, must split if exceeded\n7. **E9 - File size limit** - 500 lines per file, split by responsibility\n8. **E10 - DRY enforcement** - extract shared logic at threshold of 2\n\n### 9. cmd/od DIRECTORY STATUS\n\n**No cmd/od/ directory exists yet.** The od command has not been implemented.\n\n### 10. PATTERN SUMMARY FOR cmd/od IMPLEMENTATION\n\nFor your od implementation, follow this structure:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// Implements srd###-od [SRD description]\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"bufio\"\n    \"errors\"\n    \"flag\"\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"strings\"\n    \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\ntype options struct {\n    // Define your option flags here\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n    sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n    \n    opts, files, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n    if err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"od: %s\\n\", err)\n        os.Exit(1)\n    }\n    \n    if len(files) == 0 {\n        files = []string{\"-\"}\n    }\n    \n    exitCode := 0\n    for _, file := range files {\n        err := processFile(opts, file)\n        if err != nil {\n            fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"od: %s\\n\", err)\n            exitCode = 1\n        }\n    }\n    \n    if exitCode != 0 {\n        os.Exit(exitCode)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string, error) {\n    // Implementation\n}\n\nfunc processFile(opts options, file string) error {\n    // Implementation\n}\n```\n\n**Test structure:**\n```go\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"os/exec\"\n    \"testing\"\n    \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n    goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n    refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"god\")  // or whatever the GNU binary is named\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Skip(\"reference binary god not found\")\n    }\n    tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n        // Your test cases\n    }\n    testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e095c5d-1c7d-403b-b32d-ee3c441f5bea","uuid":"8c6e5a78-29d6-4cd7-a043-fafc2334e92d","timestamp":"2026-05-22T23:13:12.115Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I'm implementing cmd/od (octal dump) for a Go coreutils project. I need to understand:\n\n1. Look at 2-3 existing cmd/ implementations (e.g. cmd/xxd/main.go, cmd/hexdump/main.go, or any similar dump utility, or cmd/cat/main.go, cmd/wc/main.go) to understand the code patterns used: copyright header, flag parsing style, main() structure, how they use pkg/sys and pkg/testutils.\n\n2. Read pkg/sys/ to understand what functions are available (especially InstallSIGPIPEHandler).\n\n3. Read pkg/sizeparse/ to understand what it exports and how to use it.\n\n4. Look at any existing cmd/od/ directory to see if there are any files already there.\n\n5. Look at a test file (e.g. cmd/cat/cat_test.go or cmd/wc/wc_test.go) for the differential testing pattern.\n\n6. Check docs/constitutions/ for any style guides that affect code generation - specifically the go style constitution and execution constitution.\n\nReport the exact copyright header format, the flag parsing approach (pflag vs stdlib), how main.go files are structured, how test files are structured, and any relevant style constraints from constitutions. Include code snippets.","agentId":"a3642e58976e30d85","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information needed. Let me create a comprehensive summary report.\n\n## Summary Report: Go Unix Utils Code Patterns and Style Guide\n\n### 1. COPYRIGHT HEADER FORMAT\n\nAll Go files start with a two-line SPDX copyright header, followed by a blank line, then the package declaration:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n```\n\nThis applies to all Go files: cmd/, pkg/, and internal/. The header is mandatory.\n\n### 2. FLAG PARSING APPROACH\n\n**Two patterns are used depending on complexity:**\n\n**Simple utilities (cat, echo):** Manual flag parsing with custom parseFlags/applyFlag functions\n- Direct iteration through args\n- Custom loop-based parsing for short flags (-abc combines multiple single flags)\n- Simple switch statements for flag recognition\n- Used in: cmd/cat/main.go, cmd/echo/main.go\n\n**Complex utilities (numfmt, head, wc):** stdlib `flag` package for some, manual parsing for others\n- cmd/numfmt/main.go uses `flag.String`, `flag.Int`, etc. from stdlib\n- cmd/head/main.go uses custom parseLongFlag/parseShortFlags with dedicated arg handling\n- cmd/wc/main.go also uses custom parsing but with long-flag support (--lines=, --bytes=)\n- No pflag dependency; standard library only\n\nExample from cmd/cat (simple pattern):\n```go\nfunc parseFlags(args []string) []string {\n    var files []string\n    endOfFlags := false\n    for _, arg := range args {\n        if endOfFlags || arg == \"\" || arg == \"-\" || arg[0] != '-' {\n            files = append(files, arg)\n            continue\n        }\n        if arg == \"--\" {\n            endOfFlags = true\n            continue\n        }\n        for _, c := range arg[1:] {\n            applyFlag(c)\n        }\n    }\n    return files\n}\n```\n\nExample from cmd/head (more complex pattern):\n```go\nfunc parseLongFlag(flag string, remaining []string, opts *options) (int, error) {\n    switch {\n    case flag == \"--help\":\n        fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n        os.Exit(0)\n        return 0, nil\n    case strings.HasPrefix(flag, \"--lines=\"):\n        count, err := parseLineCount(flag[len(\"--lines=\"):])\n        // ... handle\n        return 1, nil\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 3. MAIN.GO STRUCTURE\n\nAll cmd/ utilities follow a consistent pattern:\n\n1. **Copyright header** (lines 1-3)\n2. **Package declaration with comment** (lines 4-6) - often includes SRD reference\n3. **Imports** (lines 8-17) - organized in groups: stdlib, then github.com packages\n4. **Global variables** (if needed) - flags and constants\n5. **func main()** - entry point:\n   - **First line**: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - critical for piping behavior\n   - Parse arguments\n   - Set defaults\n   - Call helper functions to execute work\n   - Handle errors and set exit code\n6. **Helper functions** - named, focused functions for each responsibility\n\nExample structure from cmd/cat/main.go:\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"bufio\"\n    \"errors\"\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"syscall\"\n    \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\nvar (\n    flagN bool\n    flagB bool\n    // ... other flags\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n    sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n    args := parseFlags(os.Args[1:])\n    // ... parse, execute, handle errors\n}\n\n// Helper functions follow...\n```\n\n### 4. KEY OBSERVATIONS ABOUT sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5475/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\n**Signature:**\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n    c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n    signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n    go func() {\n        <-c\n        os.Exit(0)\n    }()\n}\n```\n\n- Must be called at the start of main()\n- Matches GNU coreutils behavior when piped to consumers that close early\n- Safe to call multiple times (each invocation starts one goroutine)\n- Uses signal.Notify with buffered channel (not signal.Ignore)\n\n### 5. pkg/sizeparse EXPORTS\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5475/pkg/sizeparse/parse.go`\n\n**Key functions:**\n```go\n// ParseOptions configures size string parsing\ntype ParseOptions struct {\n    AllowSign   bool  // permits +/- prefix\n    DefaultUnit int64 // multiplier when no suffix\n}\n\n// Parse parses human-readable size (delegates to ParseWithOptions with defaults)\nfunc Parse(s string) (int64, error)\n\n// ParseWithOptions parses with configurable options\nfunc ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error)\n```\n\n**Supported suffixes:** b (512), K/KiB (1024), KB (1000), M/MiB (1<<20), MB (1M), G/GiB (1<<30), GB (1B), T/TiB (1<<40), TB, P/PiB (1<<50), PB, E/EiB (1<<60), EB\n\n**Usage example from cmd/head:**\n```go\nimport \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\"\n\nfunc parseByteCount(s string) (int64, error) {\n    n, err := sizeparse.ParseWithOptions(s, sizeparse.ParseOptions{AllowSign: true})\n    if err != nil {\n        return 0, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid number of bytes: '%s'\", s)\n    }\n    return n, nil\n}\n```\n\n### 6. TEST FILE STRUCTURE\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5475/cmd/cat/cat_test.go`\n\n**Pattern: Differential Testing**\n\n```go\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"bytes\"\n    \"context\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"os/exec\"\n    \"path/filepath\"\n    \"testing\"\n    \"time\"\n    \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n    goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n    refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gcat\")  // GNU reference with g-prefix\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Skip(\"reference binary gcat not found\")\n    }\n    tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n        {Name: \"test_name\", Stdin: []byte(\"data\")},\n        {Name: \"another_test\", Args: []string{\"-flag\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"data\")},\n        // ...\n    }\n    testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n\n// Additional non-differential tests can follow\nfunc TestSIGPIPE(t *testing.T) {\n    goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n    // ... test SIGPIPE handling\n}\n```\n\n**Key DiffTest struct fields:**\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n    Name          string        // subtest name for t.Run\n    Args          []string      // command-line args\n    Stdin         []byte        // nil = EOF immediately, []byte{} = open then close\n    Env           []string      // merged into inherited env; LC_ALL=C is default\n    WorkDir       string        // working directory (temp dir if empty)\n    ExitCode      int           // expected exit code (default 0)\n    Normalize     []NormalizeFunc // transformation funcs before comparison\n    ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte // check created files\n}\n```\n\n### 7. PACKAGE STRUCTURE (pkg/sys and pkg/testutils)\n\n**pkg/sys exports:**\n- `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - signal handling\n- `OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))` - SIGWINCH handler\n- `TerminalWidth() (int, error)` - get terminal width\n- File info helpers (fileinfo.go)\n- Platform-specific stat functions (stat_darwin.go, etc.)\n\n**pkg/testutils exports:**\n- `BuildBinary(t *testing.T, path string) string` - compile cmd package, return binary path\n- `RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)` - run differential tests\n- `DiffTest` struct - test case definition\n- `NormalizeFunc` - func([]byte) []byte for output normalization\n- `TimestampNormalizer` - built-in normalizer for timestamp tests\n- `ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc` - combine normalizers\n\n### 8. CODE STYLE CONSTRAINTS (from docs/constitutions)\n\n**From go-style.yaml:**\n\n1. **Copyright header** - mandatory on lines 1-2 before package\n2. **Duplication threshold is 2** - if code appears twice, extract to shared function\n3. **Implementation strategy** - write all files before building, plan fully, minimize turns\n4. **Function size limit (E8)** - no function may exceed 40 lines of code\n5. **File size limit (E9)** - files should stay under 500 lines; split by responsibility when exceeded\n6. **No interface{}/any** - every value must have concrete type or named interface\n7. **Small interfaces** - 1-3 methods per interface\n8. **Accept interfaces as parameters, return concrete structs**\n9. **Struct embedding for field sharing**\n10. **DRY enforcement (E10)** - extract if code repeats\n\n**From execution.yaml (critical constraints):**\n\n1. **E1 - Specification-first** - code must match SRDs and ARCHITECTURE, don't invent patterns\n2. **E2 - Traceability** - commit messages reference SRD implementations\n3. **E3 - No scope creep** - only modify listed files, no extra features\n4. **E4 - Session completion** - work complete when files written and tests pass, NO git commands\n5. **E6 - Non-goals enforcement** - don't implement features in SRD non_goals\n6. **E8 - Function size hard limit** - 40 lines max, must split if exceeded\n7. **E9 - File size limit** - 500 lines per file, split by responsibility\n8. **E10 - DRY enforcement** - extract shared logic at threshold of 2\n\n### 9. cmd/od DIRECTORY STATUS\n\n**No cmd/od/ directory exists yet.** The od command has not been implemented.\n\n### 10. PATTERN SUMMARY FOR cmd/od IMPLEMENTATION\n\nFor your od implementation, follow this structure:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// Implements srd###-od [SRD description]\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"bufio\"\n    \"errors\"\n    \"flag\"\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"io\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"strings\"\n    \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\ntype options struct {\n    // Define your option flags here\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n    sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n    \n    opts, files, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n    if err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"od: %s\\n\", err)\n        os.Exit(1)\n    }\n    \n    if len(files) == 0 {\n        files = []string{\"-\"}\n    }\n    \n    exitCode := 0\n    for _, file := range files {\n        err := processFile(opts, file)\n        if err != nil {\n            fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"od: %s\\n\", err)\n            exitCode = 1\n        }\n    }\n    \n    if exitCode != 0 {\n        os.Exit(exitCode)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string, error) {\n    // Implementation\n}\n\nfunc processFile(opts options, file string) error {\n    // Implementation\n}\n```\n\n**Test structure:**\n```go\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"os/exec\"\n    \"testing\"\n    \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n    goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n    refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"god\")  // or whatever the GNU binary is named\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Skip(\"reference binary god not found\")\n    }\n    tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n        // Your test cases\n    }\n    testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```"}],"t